    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d436">

                <pb facs="0726" n="700" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg700"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/5–554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The United States
                            Delegation to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-05T21:00:00+01:00">May 5, 1954—9 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Secto 109. Repeated information Paris 202.
                    Reference: Secto 105, repeated Paris
                        200.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d436-f1"/>
                    Chauvel states Gromyko raised objection to present three chairmen or Wan alone or any outsider or to letting nine
                    choose.</p>
                <p>He proposed rotation among five or among four (leaving out France as participant
                    in fighting), both of which Chauvel of
                    course rejected. Chauvel stated rotation
                    of UK and USSR unacceptable to French.</p>
                <p>Although he might easily have done so Gromyko made no mention of including India or additional
                    participants.</p>
                <p>Molotov dining with Eden tonight and they will discuss it further,
                    with Eden again pressing for either
                    rotation of three or Wan alone.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
